-- A function whose stopping case is never reached: counting down by 2 from 5
-- goes 3, 1, -1, and never meets 0. It reads n on every call, so it holds no
-- more memory as it goes. Its #EVAL is stopped by a limit. After a count, the
-- #EVAL after it still answers; after a time or memory limit, it is not run.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
countDown n MEANS
    IF n EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE countDown (n - 2)

#EVAL countDown 5

#EVAL 2 PLUS 2
